.TH "GMB" "1" "Aug 2026" "GlassMarble 0.1.0" "GlassMarble Manual"

.SH NAME
gmb-why - Ask a grounded architecture question (e.g. 'why is Redis used?')


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb why [question] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries the GlassMarble AI Architect with strict grounding in the
Architecture Knowledge Graph and developer memory evidence.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for why

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Emit machine-readable JSON output


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dir\fP=""
	Target repository directory for analysis and queries

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Ask why a specific technology or pattern is used
  gmb why "why was Redis selected for session storage?"

  # Ask why a service dependency exists
  gmb why "why does AuthService depend on UserStore?"

  # Ask why a technology or component is used in this repository
  gmb why "why is tree-sitter used for parsing?"

  # Output grounded answer as JSON
  gmb why "why was the v2 API introduced?" --json
.EE


